      "writtenOn": "2021-10-27T22:21:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think a better approach would be to create a separate node that lists the power signals.  The active low/active high can still be set here, but the binding to the power signals should be done in a separate node.\n\npower-signal-list { \n    ap_wdt_asserted {\n        power-enum-name \u003d \"AP_WDT_ASSERTED\";\n        gpios \u003d \u003c\u0026ap_ec_watchdog_l\u003e;\n    }\n    ap_in_s3_l {\n        power-enum-name \u003d \"AP_IN_S3_L\";\n        gpios \u003d \u003c\u0026ap_in_sleep_l\u003e;\n    }\n}\n\nSee the bb_retimer.dts file on Volteer for an example of referencing the a node from the named-gpios property.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "c213fde76491dc196303f2ce6eea81ec650d6165",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
